# Expense approval — Acme Cloud Systems

> Module Expense_approval_acme
> Using Legal_types as T

Sources: SYN-006 § 2.1 (Corporate Expense Reimbursement Policy) as the base ladder,
SYN-007 § 2.1–2.2 (Engineering Department Expense Policy), resolved by

  SYN-005 § 7.1 — A department may adopt a policy that is more restrictive than the
  Corporate Expense Reimbursement Policy. Where a department policy and the Corporate
  Expense Reimbursement Policy differ, the more restrictive approval requirement controls.

Unlike the liability cap, the resolution here is a comparison rather than a document rank,
so § 7.1 is encoded as an explicit ordering over approval levels.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope ExpenseApproval:
  input amount content money
  input department content T.Department

  internal corporate_level content T.ApprovalLevel
  internal department_level content optional of T.ApprovalLevel

  output approval_level content T.ApprovalLevel
  output receipt_required content boolean

declaration strictness content integer
  depends on level content T.ApprovalLevel
```

The ordering the handbook's "more restrictive" means, spelled out once.

```catala
declaration strictness content integer
  depends on level content T.ApprovalLevel
  equals
    match level with pattern
    -- Manager: 1
    -- Director: 2
    -- VicePresident: 3
    -- ChiefFinancialOfficer: 4
```

## SYN-006 § 2.1 — the corporate approval ladder

  $1,000.00 or less → Manager; more than $1,000.00 up to and including $5,000.00 →
  Director; more than $5,000.00 up to and including $25,000.00 → Vice President; more than
  $25,000.00 → Chief Financial Officer.

```catala
scope ExpenseApproval:
  label corporate_base
  definition corporate_level equals T.ApprovalLevel.Manager

  label corporate_director exception corporate_base
  definition corporate_level
    under condition amount > $1,000 and amount <= $5,000
    consequence equals T.ApprovalLevel.Director

  label corporate_vp exception corporate_base
  definition corporate_level
    under condition amount > $5,000 and amount <= $25,000
    consequence equals T.ApprovalLevel.VicePresident

  label corporate_cfo exception corporate_base
  definition corporate_level
    under condition amount > $25,000
    consequence equals T.ApprovalLevel.ChiefFinancialOfficer
```

## SYN-007 § 2.1–2.2 — the Engineering ladder

  All expenses over two thousand five hundred dollars ($2,500.00) require Director
  approval. Expenses of two thousand five hundred dollars ($2,500.00) or less require
  Manager approval.

The department policy exists only for Engineering; elsewhere there is nothing to compare.

```catala
scope ExpenseApproval:
  label no_department_policy
  definition department_level equals Absent

  label engineering_manager exception no_department_policy
  definition department_level
    under condition department = T.Department.Engineering and amount <= $2,500
    consequence equals Present content T.ApprovalLevel.Manager

  label engineering_director exception no_department_policy
  definition department_level
    under condition department = T.Department.Engineering and amount > $2,500
    consequence equals Present content T.ApprovalLevel.Director
```

## SYN-005 § 7.1 — the more restrictive requirement controls

```catala
scope ExpenseApproval:
  definition approval_level equals
    match department_level with pattern
    -- Present content dept:
      (if strictness of dept > strictness of corporate_level then dept
       else corporate_level)
    -- Absent: corporate_level
```

## SYN-006 § 3.1 — receipts

  An itemized receipt is required for any single expense over seventy-five dollars
  ($75.00).

```catala
scope ExpenseApproval:
  definition receipt_required equals amount > $75
```
